# Build context exclusions for image builds rooted at the repository.
#
# Docker reads .dockerignore from the context root only. controller/Dockerfile
# builds with the repository root as its context, so controller/.dockerignore
# does not apply to it and this file is what governs that build.
#
# Keep this conservative. `COPY . /workspace` feeds a Go workspace build, so
# every module directory, go.work, go.work.sum and the committed vendor/ tree
# must reach the builder. LICENSE and NOTICE are copied into the final image.
# Exclude only what the build cannot use.

# Version control.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Build output. Stale binaries from a host build would be copied in and, worse,
# invalidate the layer cache on every local rebuild.
bin/
**/bin/

# Editor and OS files.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

# Local developer configuration. controller/README.md tells contributors to
# create .env.local; it holds host-local settings and must never enter an image.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# CI definitions and documentation. Neither is read by any image build.
.github/
docs/
